VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5080
# Direct calls from the browser to climate-tracking (see web/src/features/tracking/api/trackingApi.ts).
#
# THIS ALSO SWITCHES THE TRACKING MODULE ON (#125). features/tracking/api/config.ts reads
# it as a capability flag: set to a non-blank value, the sidebar offers the tracking
# dashboards and hides the generic Action Plans entry; left blank or unset, the module's
# pages ship as chunks nothing ever navigates to. It is NOT company scoping -- the tracking
# service resolves the tenant from the caller's own JWT claim, via
# MatchingTenantRequirement(ProcomerCompanyId).
#
# The note that used to sit here said this was "inert until climate-tracking adds CORS
# support for this frontend's origin (#56 Plan B)". Half of that is out of date, and the
# other half is now a DEPLOYMENT step rather than a code one:
#   - The code landed. services/tracking-api/src/ClimateTracking.Api/Program.cs calls
#     AddCors() and registers a "Frontend" policy over WithOrigins(allowedOrigins), applied
#     by app.UseCors("Frontend"). Commit 1428241, "add CORS support for direct frontend
#     calls to tracking service".
#   - The ALLOWLIST is configuration and it ships EMPTY. appsettings.json has
#     "Cors": { "AllowedOrigins": [] }, and unlike climate-project-api there is no
#     deployment template under infra/aws/ that sets it for this service. So until the
#     tracking deployment passes Cors__AllowedOrigins__0=<this frontend's origin>, every
#     browser call from here still fails preflight: authFetch always sets Authorization
#     and Content-Type, so every request this client makes is preflighted.
# The tracking pages treat that failure as they treat any outage -- a retryable message
# inside the shell, never a broken page.
VITE_TRACKING_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5081

# OAuth client id for the "Continue with Google" button on /login (#81).
# Must be the SAME value as the API's `GoogleClientId` -- the API validates the
# ID token's audience against it. Leave empty and the button is not rendered at
# all; email + password sign-in is unaffected.
#
# The client must list <origin>/auth/loading as an authorized redirect URI.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
